/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 1 Samuel chapters 21-25
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("1samuel", [
{n:21, name:"David at Nob and Gath", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 21:9",verse:"And the priest said, The sword of Goliath the Philistine, whom thou slewest in the valley of Elah, behold, it is here wrapped in a cloth behind the ephod: if thou wilt take that, take it: for there is no other save that here. And David said, There is none like that; give it me."}, facts:["Did you know the bread Ahimelech gave David was the shewbread, the bread of the Presence kept before the LORD, and Jesus Himself later pointed to this moment to defend mercy over ritual (1 Samuel 21:6)?","Did you know Doeg the Edomite was standing by when David visited Nob, and he would soon report it all to Saul with deadly results (1 Samuel 21:7)?","Did you know Gath was Goliath's own hometown, so David fled for safety to the very city of the giant he had slain (1 Samuel 21:10)?"], questions:[
{q:"To whom did David come when he fled from Saul?", options:["Ahimelech the priest at Nob","Samuel the prophet at Ramah","Gad the seer in Judah","The king of Moab at Mizpeh"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:1",verse:"Then came David to Nob to Ahimelech the priest: and Ahimelech was afraid at the meeting of David, and said unto him, Why art thou alone, and no man with thee?", insight:"David ran to a priest before he ran anywhere else; when trouble comes, flee first to God's presence."},
{q:"How did Ahimelech receive David, and what did he ask?", options:["He was afraid at the meeting of David, and asked why he was alone","He welcomed him with a feast, and asked for news of Saul","He refused to see him, and sent him away at once","He laughed with joy, and asked where his men were"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:1",verse:"Then came David to Nob to Ahimelech the priest: and Ahimelech was afraid at the meeting of David, and said unto him, Why art thou alone, and no man with thee?", insight:"The priest's fear tells us David arrived looking hunted; God's servants often feel the weight of our crises before we speak."},
{q:"What did David say about his servants?", options:["He had appointed them to such and such a place","They were hiding in the cave of Adullam","They had gone ahead to Gath","They were with Samuel at Ramah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:2",verse:"And David said unto Ahimelech the priest, The king hath commanded me a business, and hath said unto me, Let no man know any thing of the business whereabout I send thee, and what I have commanded thee: and I have appointed my servants to such and such a place.", insight:"David's cover story included his men; lies multiply when we start inventing details."},
{q:"What excuse did David give the priest?", options:["The king hath commanded me a business, and none must know of it","Saul sent me to seek thy counsel","I am on a journey to Gath","Samuel sent me with a message"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:2",verse:"And David said unto Ahimelech the priest, The king hath commanded me a business, and hath said unto me, Let no man know any thing of the business whereabout I send thee, and what I have commanded thee: and I have appointed my servants to such and such a place.", insight:"David lied to God's priest; even the man after God's own heart stumbled when fear wrote the script."},
{q:"What did David first ask Ahimelech for?", options:["Bread, whatever was under his hand","A spear and a shield","An ass for the journey","Gold for the road"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:3",verse:"Now therefore what is under thine hand? give me five loaves of bread in mine hand, or what there is present.", insight:"Hunger humbles kings; David asked simply for bread, and God met him in the asking."},
{q:"What bread did Ahimelech have to give?", options:["Only hallowed bread, the shewbread of the Presence","Common loaves baked that morning","Bread sent from Egypt","Cakes from the altar of sacrifice"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:4",verse:"And the priest answered David, and said, There is no common bread under mine hand, but there is hallowed bread; if the young men have kept themselves at least from women.", insight:"God made room in His house for the hungry; mercy outranks ritual in the heart of God."},
{q:"On what condition was the hallowed bread given?", options:["If the young men had kept themselves from women","If David fasted three days","If David offered a sacrifice","If the bread was first blessed"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:4",verse:"And the priest answered David, and said, There is no common bread under mine hand, but there is hallowed bread; if the young men have kept themselves at least from women.", insight:"Even in crisis, holiness mattered; approaching God's table asks for a clean heart."},
{q:"What did David say of his young men?", options:["The vessels of the young men are holy","They are fasting until evening","They carry the ark of God","They are unclean from battle"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:5",verse:"And David answered the priest, and said unto him, Of a truth women have been kept from us about these three days, since I came out, and the vessels of the young men are holy, and the bread is in a manner common, yea, though it were sanctified this day in the vessel.", insight:"David appealed to the purity of his men; conscience should stay awake even in a crisis."},
{q:"Who was detained at Nob that day?", options:["Doeg, an Edomite, chiefest of the herdmen of Saul","Joab, captain of the host","Abner, commander of Saul's army","A messenger from the king"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:7",verse:"Now a certain man of the servants of Saul was there that day, detained before the LORD; and his name was Doeg, an Edomite, the chiefest of the herdmen that belonged to Saul.", insight:"Doeg watched in the shadows; God saw what the witness would do with what he saw."},
{q:"Why was Doeg at Nob?", options:["He was detained before the LORD","He was offering a sacrifice","He was healing the sick","He was buying cattle"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:7",verse:"Now a certain man of the servants of Saul was there that day, detained before the LORD; and his name was Doeg, an Edomite, the chiefest of the herdmen that belonged to Saul.", insight:"Detained before the LORD; even God's house can hold a spy, so walk wisely and purely."},
{q:"What weapon did David ask for?", options:["A spear or a sword","A bow and arrows","A sling and stones","A shield of brass"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:8",verse:"And David said unto Ahimelech, And is there not here under thine hand spear or sword? for I have neither brought my sword nor my weapons with me, because the king’s business required haste.", insight:"David fled without his sword; God provides arms even for the unarmed who trust Him."},
{q:"What sword did the priest offer David?", options:["The sword of Goliath, wrapped in a cloth behind the ephod","Saul's own royal sword","Jonathan's sword","A new Philistine blade"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:9",verse:"And the priest said, The sword of Goliath the Philistine, whom thou slewest in the valley of Elah, behold, it is here wrapped in a cloth behind the ephod: if thou wilt take that, take it: for there is no other save that here. And David said, There is none like that; give it me.", insight:"The giant's sword now served the shepherd; God turns the enemy's weapon into His servant's shield."},
{q:"What did David say when he saw Goliath's sword?", options:["There is none like that; give it me","It is too heavy for my hand","It belongs to the priest","It is unclean for battle"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:9",verse:"And the priest said, The sword of Goliath the Philistine, whom thou slewest in the valley of Elah, behold, it is here wrapped in a cloth behind the ephod: if thou wilt take that, take it: for there is no other save that here. And David said, There is none like that; give it me.", insight:"There is none like that; remembering God's past victories steadies us for present fears."},
{q:"Where did David flee after leaving Nob?", options:["To Achish the king of Gath","To the king of Moab","To Samuel at Ramah","To the wilderness of Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:10",verse:"And David arose, and fled that day for fear of Saul, and went to Achish the king of Gath.", insight:"Fear drove David to Gath, the giant's hometown; desperation sends us to strange places."},
{q:"How did the servants of Achish recognize David?", options:["They sang of him: Saul hath slain his thousands, and David his ten thousands","They had seen him at Nob","A servant betrayed him","They read his letter"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:11",verse:"And the servants of Achish said unto him, Is not this David the king of the land? did they not sing one to another of him in dances, saying, Saul hath slain his thousands, and David his ten thousands?", insight:"Fame followed David into enemy land; our past is known in places we never expect."},
{q:"What did David do with their words?", options:["He laid them up in his heart, and was sore afraid","He laughed them off","He challenged them to fight","He fled at once"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:12",verse:"And David laid up these words in his heart, and was sore afraid of Achish the king of Gath.", insight:"David treasured the threat in his heart; fear grows when we hide it instead of taking it to God."},
{q:"How did David disguise himself before Achish?", options:["He changed his behaviour and feigned himself mad","He dressed as a merchant","He dyed his hair grey","He wore Saul's armor"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:13",verse:"And he changed his behaviour before them, and feigned himself mad in their hands, and scrabbled on the doors of the gate, and let his spittle fall down upon his beard.", insight:"The anointed king played the madman; pride must sometimes bow low to survive."},
{q:"What signs of madness did David show?", options:["He scrabbled on the doors of the gate and let his spittle fall on his beard","He howled like a wolf","He tore his clothes","He ran through the streets"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:13",verse:"And he changed his behaviour before them, and feigned himself mad in their hands, and scrabbled on the doors of the gate, and let his spittle fall down upon his beard.", insight:"Scribbling on doors and drooling; God let David's dignity break to keep his life whole."},
{q:"What did Achish say of David?", options:["Lo, ye see the man is mad","He is a mighty warrior","Bring him food and rest","Bind him in chains"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:14",verse:"Then said Achish unto his servants, Lo, ye see the man is mad: wherefore then have ye brought him to me?", insight:"Achish saw madness and missed the king; God's disguise protects His own."},
{q:"Why did Achish refuse to take David in?", options:["Have I need of mad men? Shall this fellow come into my house?","David was too strong","The Philistines feared him","Saul had warned him"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 21:15",verse:"Have I need of mad men, that ye have brought this fellow to play the mad man in my presence? shall this fellow come into my house?", insight:"God shut the door of Gath; when God closes a door, He is opening a cave of refuge."}
]},
{n:22, name:"Slaughter at Nob", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 22:23",verse:"Abide thou with me, fear not: for he that seeketh my life seeketh thy life: but with me thou shalt be in safeguard."}, facts:["Did you know David's first army was made of the distressed, the debtors, and the discontented, about four hundred outcasts who became his mighty men (1 Samuel 22:2)?","Did you know Saul's own footmen refused to strike the priests, so the slaughter was carried out by Doeg the Edomite, a foreigner (1 Samuel 22:17-18)?","Did you know Abiathar's escape brought the ephod to David, giving him the means to inquire of God before every battle from then on (1 Samuel 22:20; 23:6)?"], questions:[
{q:"Where did David escape after leaving Gath?", options:["The cave Adullam","The forest of Hareth","The wilderness of Ziph","The strong holds of Engedi"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:1",verse:"David therefore departed thence, and escaped to the cave Adullam: and when his brethren and all his father’s house heard it, they went down thither to him.", insight:"A cave became David's first palace; God hides His kings before He crowns them."},
{q:"Who gathered themselves to David at Adullam?", options:["Every one in distress, in debt, and discontented","The priests of Nob","Saul's captains","The elders of Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:2",verse:"And every one that was in distress, and every one that was in debt, and every one that was discontented, gathered themselves unto him; and he became a captain over them: and there were with him about four hundred men.", insight:"God built David's army from broken people; He still recruits the distressed, not the impressive."},
{q:"How many men gathered to David?", options:["About four hundred","About forty","About four thousand","About twelve"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:2",verse:"And every one that was in distress, and every one that was in debt, and every one that was discontented, gathered themselves unto him; and he became a captain over them: and there were with him about four hundred men.", insight:"Four hundred nobodies became mighty men; small, surrendered beginnings grow great in God's hands."},
{q:"Where did David take his father and mother for safety?", options:["To the king of Moab at Mizpeh","To Samuel at Ramah","To the priests at Nob","To Jesse at Bethlehem"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:3",verse:"And David went thence to Mizpeh of Moab: and he said unto the king of Moab, Let my father and my mother, I pray thee, come forth, and be with you, till I know what God will do for me.", insight:"Even in flight, David honored his parents; caring for family is part of trusting God."},
{q:"What did David want to know while his parents stayed in Moab?", options:["What God would do for him","Where Saul was hiding","When the war would end","How to pay the king"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:3",verse:"And David went thence to Mizpeh of Moab: and he said unto the king of Moab, Let my father and my mother, I pray thee, come forth, and be with you, till I know what God will do for me.", insight:"Till I know what God will do for me; waiting on God's plan is itself an act of faith."},
{q:"What did the prophet Gad tell David?", options:["Abide not in the hold; depart into the land of Judah","Stay in the cave of Adullam","Flee to Egypt","Go up to Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:5",verse:"And the prophet Gad said unto David, Abide not in the hold; depart, and get thee into the land of Judah. Then David departed, and came into the forest of Hareth.", insight:"God sent a prophet to move David; guidance often comes through God's messengers, not just our instincts."},
{q:"Where did David go at Gad's word?", options:["The forest of Hareth","The wilderness of Paran","The mount of Olives","The plains of Moab"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:5",verse:"And the prophet Gad said unto David, Abide not in the hold; depart, and get thee into the land of Judah. Then David departed, and came into the forest of Hareth.", insight:"David obeyed the hard word and left his hiding place; safety is found in obedience, not in caves."},
{q:"Where was Saul when he heard of David?", options:["Under a tree in Ramah, his spear in his hand","In his palace at Gibeah","At the tabernacle in Nob","On the battlefield"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:6",verse:"When Saul heard that David was discovered, and the men that were with him, (now Saul abode in Gibeah under a tree in Ramah, having his spear in his hand, and all his servants were standing about him;)", insight:"Saul sat clutching his spear; suspicion had become his constant companion."},
{q:"What did Saul accuse his servants of?", options:["Conspiring with David, while his son made a league with him","Stealing from the treasury","Worshipping idols","Plotting to kill him"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:8",verse:"That all of you have conspired against me, and there is none that sheweth me that my son hath made a league with the son of Jesse, and there is none of you that is sorry for me, or sheweth unto me that my son hath stirred up my servant against me, to lie in wait, as at this day?", insight:"Guilt sees conspiracies everywhere; a troubled conscience accuses even the innocent."},
{q:"Who answered Saul and reported on David?", options:["Doeg the Edomite","Abner the captain","A priest of Nob","A shepherd boy"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:9",verse:"Then answered Doeg the Edomite, which was set over the servants of Saul, and said, I saw the son of Jesse coming to Nob, to Ahimelech the son of Ahitub.", insight:"Doeg had waited for his moment; beware the watcher who stores up what he sees to use it later."},
{q:"What did Doeg say Ahimelech had done for David?", options:["Inquired of the LORD for him, gave him victuals and Goliath's sword","Hidden him in the tabernacle","Crowned him king","Given him an army"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:10",verse:"And he enquired of the LORD for him, and gave him victuals, and gave him the sword of Goliath the Philistine.", insight:"Doeg told the truth with a murderer's intent; facts in cruel hands become weapons."},
{q:"Whom did Saul summon to answer the charge?", options:["Ahimelech and all his father's house, the priests at Nob","The elders of Israel","David's captains","The men of Keilah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:11",verse:"Then the king sent to call Ahimelech the priest, the son of Ahitub, and all his father’s house, the priests that were in Nob: and they came all of them to the king.", insight:"An innocent priesthood was dragged to court; power drunk on fear spares no one."},
{q:"What did Saul charge Ahimelech with?", options:["Conspiracy: giving David bread and a sword, that he should rise against Saul","Stealing the shewbread","Hiding the ark","Cursing the king"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:13",verse:"And Saul said unto him, Why have ye conspired against me, thou and the son of Jesse, in that thou hast given him bread, and a sword, and hast enquired of God for him, that he should rise against me, to lie in wait, as at this day?", insight:"Kindness to David was called treason; the world often misnames mercy."},
{q:"How did Ahimelech defend David?", options:["Who is so faithful among all thy servants as David?","David never came to Nob","The king commanded it","I do not know David"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:14",verse:"Then Ahimelech answered the king, and said, And who is so faithful among all thy servants as David, which is the king’s son in law, and goeth at thy bidding, and is honourable in thine house?", insight:"Ahimelech spoke the truth about David's record; a clear conscience speaks plainly, even before kings."},
{q:"What did Ahimelech say about inquiring of God for David?", options:["Did I then begin to inquire of God for him? Be it far from me","I inquired for him daily","The LORD commanded me","I never inquire of God"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:15",verse:"Did I then begin to enquire of God for him? be it far from me: let not the king impute any thing unto his servant, nor to all the house of my father: for thy servant knew nothing of all this, less or more.", insight:"Be it far from me; the priest's honest denial shows a clean heart under false charge."},
{q:"What sentence did Saul pronounce?", options:["Thou shalt surely die, Ahimelech, thou, and all thy father's house","Thou art banished from Nob","Thy priesthood is ended","Pay a fine of silver"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:16",verse:"And the king said, Thou shalt surely die, Ahimelech, thou, and all thy father’s house.", insight:"Thou shalt surely die; rage had replaced justice on Saul's throne."},
{q:"How did Saul's footmen answer his command to slay the priests?", options:["They would not put forth their hand against the priests of the LORD","They obeyed at once","They fled from Saul","They asked for payment"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:17",verse:"And the king said unto the footmen that stood about him, Turn, and slay the priests of the LORD; because their hand also is with David, and because they knew when he fled, and did not shew it to me. But the servants of the king would not put forth their hand to fall upon the priests of the LORD.", insight:"The soldiers feared God more than the king; conscience outranks command."},
{q:"Who carried out the slaughter, and how many priests died?", options:["Doeg the Edomite slew fourscore and five","Abner slew threescore","The Philistines slew a hundred","Saul slew fifty himself"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:18",verse:"And the king said to Doeg, Turn thou, and fall upon the priests. And Doeg the Edomite turned, and he fell upon the priests, and slew on that day fourscore and five persons that did wear a linen ephod.", insight:"Eighty-five priests fell by one foreigner's hand; unchecked envy ends in atrocity."},
{q:"What happened to Nob, the city of the priests?", options:["Saul smote it with the edge of the sword, people and livestock","It was burned with fire","It was given to the Philistines","It was spared"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:19",verse:"And Nob, the city of the priests, smote he with the edge of the sword, both men and women, children and sucklings, and oxen, and asses, and sheep, with the edge of the sword.", insight:"Nob paid for David's visit; our choices ripple further than we see, so choose prayerfully."},
{q:"What did David promise Abiathar, the one priest who escaped?", options:["Abide thou with me; with me thou shalt be in safeguard","Flee to Egypt","Hide in the cave","Return to Nob"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 22:23",verse:"Abide thou with me, fear not: for he that seeketh my life seeketh thy life: but with me thou shalt be in safeguard.", insight:"With me thou shalt be in safeguard; David owned his part in the tragedy and turned it into shelter."}
]},
{n:23, name:"Keilah and the Pursuit", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 23:14",verse:"And David abode in the wilderness in strong holds, and remained in a mountain in the wilderness of Ziph. And Saul sought him every day, but God delivered him not into his hand."}, facts:["Did you know David inquired of the LORD twice before rescuing Keilah, asking and then asking again after his men feared, a pattern of double-checking with God (1 Samuel 23:2-4)?","Did you know the place where Saul broke off his pursuit was named Selahammahlekoth, the rock of divisions, for the mountain that stood between Saul and David (1 Samuel 23:28)?","Did you know Jonathan's last meeting with David was in the wood of Ziph, where he strengthened David's hand in God and yielded the throne to him (1 Samuel 23:16-18)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who was attacking Keilah when David heard of it?", options:["The Philistines, robbing the threshingfloors","The Amalekites, burning the fields","The Moabites, stealing cattle","Saul's men, seeking David"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:1",verse:"Then they told David, saying, Behold, the Philistines fight against Keilah, and they rob the threshingfloors.", insight:"The Philistines robbed the threshingfloors; even while hunted, David cared about others' harvests."},
{q:"What did David ask the LORD about Keilah?", options:["Shall I go and smite these Philistines?","Shall I flee to Moab?","Shall I hide in the cave?","Shall I send my men alone?"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:2",verse:"Therefore David enquired of the LORD, saying, Shall I go and smite these Philistines? And the LORD said unto David, Go, and smite the Philistines, and save Keilah.", insight:"David asked before he acted; prayer first is the habit that made him great."},
{q:"What did the LORD answer?", options:["Go and smite the Philistines, and save Keilah","Stay hidden in the wilderness","Wait until Saul departs","Send to the king for help"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:2",verse:"Therefore David enquired of the LORD, saying, Shall I go and smite these Philistines? And the LORD said unto David, Go, and smite the Philistines, and save Keilah.", insight:"Go and save Keilah; God's answers send us toward need, not away from it."},
{q:"Why did David's men hesitate to go?", options:["They were afraid","They were weary","They had no weapons","They distrusted David"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:3",verse:"And David’s men said unto him, Behold, we be afraid here in Judah: how much more then if we come to Keilah against the armies of the Philistines?", insight:"Behold, we be afraid; honest fear spoken aloud can be carried to God."},
{q:"In what order did David seek God's guidance about Keilah?", options:["He asked, his men feared, so he asked the LORD again","He asked twice at once","He asked only after the battle","He never asked at all"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:4",verse:"Then David enquired of the LORD yet again. And the LORD answered him and said, Arise, go down to Keilah; for I will deliver the Philistines into thine hand.", insight:"He inquired yet again; godly leaders recheck with God instead of rushing ahead."},
{q:"What promise did the LORD give the second time?", options:["I will deliver the Philistines into thine hand","Saul will die tomorrow","Keilah will fall","Thy men will fail thee"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:4",verse:"Then David enquired of the LORD yet again. And the LORD answered him and said, Arise, go down to Keilah; for I will deliver the Philistines into thine hand.", insight:"I will deliver them into thine hand; God's promise, not our courage, wins the battle."},
{q:"What did David do to the Philistines at Keilah?", options:["He smote them with a great slaughter and took their cattle","He drove them off with stones","He made peace with them","He paid them tribute"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:5",verse:"So David and his men went to Keilah, and fought with the Philistines, and brought away their cattle, and smote them with a great slaughter. So David saved the inhabitants of Keilah.", insight:"A great slaughter and rescued cattle; obedience turned fear into victory."},
{q:"What did Abiathar bring when he fled to David at Keilah?", options:["An ephod in his hand","The ark of the covenant","The tables of stone","Goliath's sword"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:6",verse:"And it came to pass, when Abiathar the son of Ahimelech fled to David to Keilah, that he came down with an ephod in his hand.", insight:"The ephod came to David in his need; God equips His servants for the very guidance they require."},
{q:"What did Saul say when he heard David was in Keilah?", options:["God hath delivered him into mine hand; he is shut in by gates and bars","David has escaped me again","The LORD has forsaken David","Keilah belongs to me now"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:7",verse:"And it was told Saul that David was come to Keilah. And Saul said, God hath delivered him into mine hand; for he is shut in, by entering into a town that hath gates and bars.", insight:"God hath delivered him; Saul mistook God's providence for his own opportunity."},
{q:"What did David ask Abiathar to bring?", options:["The ephod","The sword","The bread","The ark"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:9",verse:"And David knew that Saul secretly practised mischief against him; and he said to Abiathar the priest, Bring hither the ephod.", insight:"Bring hither the ephod; before every move, David reached for God's guidance."},
{q:"What did the LORD say when David asked if Saul would come down?", options:["He will come down","He will stay in Gibeah","He will send Abner","He will repent"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:11",verse:"Will the men of Keilah deliver me up into his hand? will Saul come down, as thy servant hath heard? O LORD God of Israel, I beseech thee, tell thy servant. And the LORD said, He will come down.", insight:"He will come down; God tells the truth about danger so we can act wisely."},
{q:"What did the LORD say about the men of Keilah?", options:["They will deliver thee up","They will fight for thee","They will hide thee","They will flee with thee"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:12",verse:"Then said David, Will the men of Keilah deliver me and my men into the hand of Saul? And the LORD said, They will deliver thee up.", insight:"They will deliver thee up; gratitude is fickle, so trust God, not the crowd."},
{q:"How many men departed out of Keilah with David?", options:["About six hundred","About four hundred","About three thousand","About sixty"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:13",verse:"Then David and his men, which were about six hundred, arose and departed out of Keilah, and went whithersoever they could go. And it was told Saul that David was escaped from Keilah; and he forbare to go forth.", insight:"Six hundred now, up from four hundred; God keeps adding to those who walk with Him."},
{q:"Where did David stay after leaving Keilah?", options:["In the wilderness of Ziph, in a wood","In the cave of Adullam","In the city of Nob","In the land of Moab"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:15",verse:"And David saw that Saul was come out to seek his life: and David was in the wilderness of Ziph in a wood.", insight:"The wilderness of Ziph in a wood; God hid His future king among the trees."},
{q:"What is said of Saul's pursuit of David?", options:["He sought him every day, but God delivered him not into his hand","He gave up after a week","He sent only spies","He forgot about David"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:14",verse:"And David abode in the wilderness in strong holds, and remained in a mountain in the wilderness of Ziph. And Saul sought him every day, but God delivered him not into his hand.", insight:"Sought every day, yet God delivered him not; no pursuit outruns God's protection."},
{q:"Who came to David in the wood of Ziph?", options:["Jonathan, Saul's son","Abner the captain","Gad the prophet","Samuel"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:16",verse:"And Jonathan Saul’s son arose, and went to David into the wood, and strengthened his hand in God.", insight:"Jonathan came into the wood; true friendship walks into danger to find you."},
{q:"What did Jonathan do for David?", options:["He strengthened his hand in God","He brought him an army","He warned him to flee","He gave him Saul's spear"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:16",verse:"And Jonathan Saul’s son arose, and went to David into the wood, and strengthened his hand in God.", insight:"Strengthened his hand in God; the greatest gift a friend gives is renewed faith."},
{q:"What did Jonathan say about the kingdom?", options:["Thou shalt be king over Israel, and I shall be next unto thee","I will be king and thou my captain","Saul will keep the throne","We will divide the kingdom"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:17",verse:"And he said unto him, Fear not: for the hand of Saul my father shall not find thee; and thou shalt be king over Israel, and I shall be next unto thee; and that also Saul my father knoweth.", insight:"Thou shalt be king; Jonathan yielded the crown with grace, and God honored his humility."},
{q:"Who told Saul where David was hiding?", options:["The Ziphites","The men of Keilah","Doeg the Edomite","The Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:19",verse:"Then came up the Ziphites to Saul to Gibeah, saying, Doth not David hide himself with us in strong holds in the wood, in the hill of Hachilah, which is on the south of Jeshimon?", insight:"The Ziphites betrayed him; not every neighbor is a friend, so lean on God."},
{q:"What stopped Saul's pursuit at Maon?", options:["A messenger brought news that the Philistines had invaded the land","His army mutinied","David surrendered","A storm arose"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 23:27",verse:"But there came a messenger unto Saul, saying, Haste thee, and come; for the Philistines have invaded the land.", insight:"God used Israel's enemies to save His anointed; Providence writes strange rescue plans."}
]},
{n:24, name:"David Spares Saul", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 24:12",verse:"The LORD judge between me and thee, and the LORD avenge me of thee: but mine hand shall not be upon thee."}, facts:["Did you know 'to cover his feet' is a Hebrew euphemism for relieving himself, which is why Saul walked unguarded into a cave full of armed men (1 Samuel 24:3)?","Did you know David's men quoted a supposed promise of God to justify killing Saul, but David refused to act on a word he had never received (1 Samuel 24:4)?","Did you know Saul himself confessed in the cave's aftermath that David would surely be king, the first time he admitted the future he was fighting (1 Samuel 24:20)?"], questions:[
{q:"Where was David when Saul returned from fighting the Philistines?", options:["In the wilderness of Engedi","In the cave of Adullam","In the forest of Hareth","In the city of Keilah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:1",verse:"And it came to pass, when Saul was returned from following the Philistines, that it was told him, saying, Behold, David is in the wilderness of En-gedi.", insight:"The wilderness of Engedi; God kept moving David to new hiding places."},
{q:"How many chosen men did Saul take to seek David?", options:["Three thousand","Three hundred","Thirty thousand","Three hundred thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:2",verse:"Then Saul took three thousand chosen men out of all Israel, and went to seek David and his men upon the rocks of the wild goats.", insight:"Three thousand chosen men against one fugitive; fear multiplies its forces."},
{q:"Why did Saul enter the cave by the sheepcotes?", options:["To cover his feet","To rest his army","To offer sacrifice","To hide from David"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:3",verse:"And he came to the sheepcotes by the way, where was a cave; and Saul went in to cover his feet: and David and his men remained in the sides of the cave.", insight:"To cover his feet; God arranged the moment in the most ordinary, unguarded way."},
{q:"Where were David and his men when Saul entered?", options:["In the sides of the cave","On the hill above","In the sheepcotes","Across the valley"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:3",verse:"And he came to the sheepcotes by the way, where was a cave; and Saul went in to cover his feet: and David and his men remained in the sides of the cave.", insight:"In the sides of the cave; the hunter walked into the hands of the hunted."},
{q:"What did David's men say about that day?", options:["Behold the day of which the LORD said, I will deliver thine enemy into thine hand","Saul has come to make peace","Let us flee while we can","God has forsaken Saul"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:4",verse:"And the men of David said unto him, Behold the day of which the LORD said unto thee, Behold, I will deliver thine enemy into thine hand, that thou mayest do to him as it shall seem good unto thee. Then David arose, and cut off the skirt of Saul’s robe privily.", insight:"They claimed a promise God never gave; test every counsel, even from friends, by God's voice."},
{q:"What did David do to Saul in the cave?", options:["He cut off the skirt of Saul's robe privily","He took Saul's spear","He bound Saul's hands","He woke Saul gently"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:4",verse:"And the men of David said unto him, Behold the day of which the LORD said unto thee, Behold, I will deliver thine enemy into thine hand, that thou mayest do to him as it shall seem good unto thee. Then David arose, and cut off the skirt of Saul’s robe privily.", insight:"He cut only the skirt; restraint in the moment of power is the mark of a godly heart."},
{q:"Why did David's heart smite him afterward?", options:["Because he had cut off Saul's skirt","Because he had spared Saul","Because he had lied","Because he had fled"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:5",verse:"And it came to pass afterward, that David’s heart smote him, because he had cut off Saul’s skirt.", insight:"His heart smote him; a tender conscience is God's alarm, and David listened."},
{q:"What did David say about touching Saul?", options:["The LORD forbid that I should stretch forth mine hand against the LORD's anointed","Saul deserves death","My men command it","The time is not yet"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:6",verse:"And he said unto his men, The LORD forbid that I should do this thing unto my master, the LORD’S anointed, to stretch forth mine hand against him, seeing he is the anointed of the LORD.", insight:"The LORD forbid; David honored God's anointing even when the anointed was unjust."},
{q:"What did David not allow his servants to do?", options:["He suffered them not to rise against Saul","He would not let them eat","He kept them from speaking","He stopped them from leaving"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:7",verse:"So David stayed his servants with these words, and suffered them not to rise against Saul. But Saul rose up out of the cave, and went on his way.", insight:"He stayed his servants with words; a leader's restraint protects others from sin."},
{q:"How did David present himself to Saul outside the cave?", options:["He cried, My lord the king, and bowed with his face to the earth","He stood with sword drawn","He fled into the hills","He sent a messenger"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:8",verse:"David also arose afterward, and went out of the cave, and cried after Saul, saying, My lord the king. And when Saul looked behind him, David stooped with his face to the earth, and bowed himself.", insight:"He bowed to the earth; humility disarms better than any weapon."},
{q:"What did David ask Saul?", options:["Wherefore hearest thou men's words, saying, David seeketh thy hurt?","Why dost thou pursue me?","Wilt thou make peace?","Who told thee I was here?"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:9",verse:"And David said to Saul, Wherefore hearest thou men’s words, saying, Behold, David seeketh thy hurt?", insight:"Wherefore hearest thou men's words? David named the real enemy: slander."},
{q:"How did David describe God's part that day?", options:["The LORD had delivered Saul into David's hand, yet he killed him not","God had hidden David","God had blinded Saul","God had sent an angel"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:10",verse:"Behold, this day thine eyes have seen how that the LORD had delivered thee to day into mine hand in the cave: and some bade me kill thee: but mine eye spared thee; and I said, I will not put forth mine hand against my lord; for he is the LORD’S anointed.", insight:"God delivered Saul into his hand; David saw the moment as a test, not a prize."},
{q:"What proof did David hold up to Saul?", options:["The skirt of Saul's robe in his hand","Saul's spear","Saul's crown","A lock of Saul's hair"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:11",verse:"Moreover, my father, see, yea, see the skirt of thy robe in my hand: for in that I cut off the skirt of thy robe and killed thee not, know thou and see that there is neither evil nor transgression in mine hand, and I have not sinned against thee; yet thou huntest my soul to take it.", insight:"See the skirt; evidence of mercy speaks louder than claims of loyalty."},
{q:"What did David say some had urged him to do?", options:["Some bade me kill thee, but mine eye spared thee","Some bade me flee, but I stayed","Some bade me hide, but I came out","Some bade me fight, but I yielded"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:11",verse:"Moreover, my father, see, yea, see the skirt of thy robe in my hand: for in that I cut off the skirt of thy robe and killed thee not, know thou and see that there is neither evil nor transgression in mine hand, and I have not sinned against thee; yet thou huntest my soul to take it.", insight:"Mine eye spared thee; mercy chosen under pressure is mercy indeed."},
{q:"What did David leave in the LORD's hands?", options:["The LORD judge between me and thee, and the LORD avenge me; but mine hand shall not be upon thee","The kingdom and the crown","His men and his sword","The cave and the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:12",verse:"The LORD judge between me and thee, and the LORD avenge me of thee: but mine hand shall not be upon thee.", insight:"The LORD judge between me and thee; David handed his case to the highest court."},
{q:"What proverb of the ancients did David quote?", options:["Wickedness proceedeth from the wicked","Pride goeth before a fall","A soft answer turneth away wrath","The fear of man bringeth a snare"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:13",verse:"As saith the proverb of the ancients, Wickedness proceedeth from the wicked: but mine hand shall not be upon thee.", insight:"Wickedness proceedeth from the wicked; our actions reveal our hearts, so David kept his clean."},
{q:"To what did David compare himself before the king?", options:["A dead dog, a flea","A lion of Judah","A mighty warrior","A servant of the king"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:14",verse:"After whom is the king of Israel come out? after whom dost thou pursue? after a dead dog, after a flea.", insight:"A dead dog, a flea; David's lowliness was honest, and God lifts the humble."},
{q:"How did Saul respond to David's words?", options:["He lifted up his voice and wept","He laughed","He ordered his arrest","He walked away silent"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:16",verse:"And it came to pass, when David had made an end of speaking these words unto Saul, that Saul said, Is this thy voice, my son David? And Saul lifted up his voice, and wept.", insight:"Saul wept; even hard hearts can crack when mercy confronts them."},
{q:"What did Saul confess to David?", options:["Thou art more righteous than I; thou hast rewarded me good, whereas I have rewarded thee evil","Thou art a traitor","I will kill thee yet","Thou hast deceived me"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:17",verse:"And he said to David, Thou art more righteous than I: for thou hast rewarded me good, whereas I have rewarded thee evil.", insight:"Thou art more righteous than I; confession is the first step back, and Saul took it."},
{q:"What oath did Saul ask of David?", options:["That David would not cut off Saul's seed after him","That David would serve Saul","That David would leave Israel","That David would spare the priests"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 24:21",verse:"Swear now therefore unto me by the LORD, that thou wilt not cut off my seed after me, and that thou wilt not destroy my name out of my father’s house.", insight:"Swear thou wilt not cut off my seed; even in parting, Saul thought of his house, and David swore in kindness."}
]},
{n:25, name:"Abigail", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 25:29",verse:"Yet a man is risen to pursue thee, and to seek thy soul: but the soul of my lord shall be bound in the bundle of life with the LORD thy God; and the souls of thine enemies, them shall he sling out, as out of the middle of a sling."}, facts:["Did you know the name Nabal means fool, and Abigail told David to his face that her husband lived up to it: 'Nabal is his name, and folly is with him' (1 Samuel 25:25)?","Did you know Abigail's peace offering was enormous: two hundred loaves, five sheep, and hundreds of cakes of figs and raisins, all loaded on donkeys (1 Samuel 25:18)?","Did you know David later said Abigail's counsel kept him from bloodguilt, one of the rare moments in Scripture where a man credits a woman with saving him from his own sword (1 Samuel 25:33)?"], questions:[
{q:"What great loss opened this chapter?", options:["Samuel died, and all Israel lamented and buried him at Ramah","Saul died in battle","Jonathan was slain","Eli died at Shiloh"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:1",verse:"And Samuel died; and all the Israelites were gathered together, and lamented him, and buried him in his house at Ramah. And David arose, and went down to the wilderness of Paran.", insight:"Samuel died and all Israel lamented; the nation mourned the prophet who had anointed its kings."},
{q:"How many sheep and goats did Nabal own?", options:["Three thousand sheep and a thousand goats","Three hundred sheep and a hundred goats","Thirty thousand sheep","Three thousand goats only"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:2",verse:"And there was a man in Maon, whose possessions were in Carmel; and the man was very great, and he had three thousand sheep, and a thousand goats: and he was shearing his sheep in Carmel.", insight:"Great wealth, small heart; riches never made a fool wise."},
{q:"How is Abigail described?", options:["A woman of good understanding, and of a beautiful countenance","A woman of great wealth","A prophetess of the LORD","A daughter of the king"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:3",verse:"Now the name of the man was Nabal; and the name of his wife Abigail: and she was a woman of good understanding, and of a beautiful countenance: but the man was churlish and evil in his doings; and he was of the house of Caleb.", insight:"Good understanding and beautiful; Abigail's wisdom outshone her beauty, and God used both."},
{q:"How is Nabal described?", options:["Churlish and evil in his doings","Generous and kind","Wise and just","Poor and humble"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:3",verse:"Now the name of the man was Nabal; and the name of his wife Abigail: and she was a woman of good understanding, and of a beautiful countenance: but the man was churlish and evil in his doings; and he was of the house of Caleb.", insight:"Churlish and evil; character, not possessions, defines a man before God."},
{q:"How many young men did David send to Nabal?", options:["Ten","Twelve","Five","Forty"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:5",verse:"And David sent out ten young men, and David said unto the young men, Get you up to Carmel, and go to Nabal, and greet him in my name:", insight:"Ten young men went in peace; David's request was courteous before it was urgent."},
{q:"What greeting did David's men carry to Nabal?", options:["Peace be to thee, and to thine house, and to all that thou hast","War be upon thy house","Give us thy flocks","Saul sends his regards"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:6",verse:"And thus shall ye say to him that liveth in prosperity, Peace be both to thee, and peace be to thine house, and peace be unto all that thou hast.", insight:"Peace to thee and thine house; David came blessing before he came asking."},
{q:"What did David ask of Nabal?", options:["Whatsoever cometh to thine hand, for thy servants and thy son David","Half of thy flocks","A thousand pieces of silver","Thy finest sheep"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:8",verse:"Ask thy young men, and they will shew thee. Wherefore let the young men find favour in thine eyes: for we come in a good day: give, I pray thee, whatsoever cometh to thine hand unto thy servants, and to thy son David.", insight:"Whatsoever cometh to thine hand; David asked modestly, trusting God for the outcome."},
{q:"How did Nabal answer David's men?", options:["Who is David? Who is the son of Jesse? Many servants break away from their masters","Gladly, take what you need","Come back tomorrow","Ask Saul, not me"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:10",verse:"And Nabal answered David’s servants, and said, Who is David? and who is the son of Jesse? there be many servants now a days that break away every man from his master.", insight:"Who is David? Contempt answered courtesy; pride cannot recognize God's anointed."},
{q:"What did Nabal refuse to share?", options:["His bread, his water, and his flesh killed for the shearers","His wine cellar","His gold","His tents"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:11",verse:"Shall I then take my bread, and my water, and my flesh that I have killed for my shearers, and give it unto men, whom I know not whence they be?", insight:"My bread, my water; Nabal's 'mine' shut out mercy, and mercy shut him out."},
{q:"What did David command when his men returned?", options:["Gird ye on every man his sword","Return to the wilderness","Forgive Nabal","Send more messengers"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:13",verse:"And David said unto his men, Gird ye on every man his sword. And they girded on every man his sword; and David also girded on his sword: and there went up after David about four hundred men; and two hundred abode by the stuff.", insight:"Gird on every man his sword; wounded pride reached for the sword before it reached for God."},
{q:"How many men went with David against Nabal?", options:["About four hundred went, and two hundred stayed by the stuff","All six hundred went","Only ten went","David went alone"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:13",verse:"And David said unto his men, Gird ye on every man his sword. And they girded on every man his sword; and David also girded on his sword: and there went up after David about four hundred men; and two hundred abode by the stuff.", insight:"Four hundred went, two hundred stayed; even in anger, David kept order in his ranks."},
{q:"What did a servant tell Abigail about Nabal?", options:["He is such a son of Belial that a man cannot speak to him","He is generous","He is away from home","He has repented"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:17",verse:"Now therefore know and consider what thou wilt do; for evil is determined against our master, and against all his household: for he is such a son of Belial, that a man cannot speak to him.", insight:"A man cannot speak to him; folly seals its ears, and the household suffers."},
{q:"What did Abigail load on donkeys for David?", options:["Two hundred loaves, two bottles of wine, five sheep, parched corn, raisins, and fig cakes","Gold and silver","Weapons and armor","Fine clothing"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:18",verse:"Then Abigail made haste, and took two hundred loaves, and two bottles of wine, and five sheep ready dressed, and five measures of parched corn, and an hundred clusters of raisins, and two hundred cakes of figs, and laid them on asses.", insight:"Abigail made haste with plenty; wisdom acts quickly and generously."},
{q:"How did Abigail approach David?", options:["She fell at his feet","She stood at a distance","She sent a servant","She waited by the road"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:24",verse:"And fell at his feet, and said, Upon me, my lord, upon me let this iniquity be: and let thine handmaid, I pray thee, speak in thine audience, and hear the words of thine handmaid.", insight:"She fell at his feet; humility opened the door that Nabal's pride had slammed."},
{q:"What did Abigail say of her husband's name?", options:["Nabal is his name, and folly is with him","His name is honorable","He is wiser than he seems","His name means prince"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:25",verse:"Let not my lord, I pray thee, regard this man of Belial, even Nabal: for as his name is, so is he; Nabal is his name, and folly is with him: but I thine handmaid saw not the young men of my lord, whom thou didst send.", insight:"Nabal is his name, and folly is with him; Abigail named the truth plainly to save her house."},
{q:"What did Abigail say the LORD had done for David?", options:["The LORD hath withholden thee from coming to shed blood","The LORD hath given thee Nabal's house","The LORD hath made thee king","The LORD hath punished Saul"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:26",verse:"Now therefore, my lord, as the LORD liveth, and as thy soul liveth, seeing the LORD hath withholden thee from coming to shed blood, and from avenging thyself with thine own hand, now let thine enemies, and they that seek evil to my lord, be as Nabal.", insight:"The LORD hath withholden thee; God uses wise counsel to stop our worst impulses."},
{q:"What future did Abigail speak over David?", options:["The LORD will certainly make my lord a sure house","Thou shalt die in the wilderness","Saul shall prevail","Thy sons shall be slaves"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:28",verse:"I pray thee, forgive the trespass of thine handmaid: for the LORD will certainly make my lord a sure house; because my lord fighteth the battles of the LORD, and evil hath not been found in thee all thy days.", insight:"A sure house; Abigail saw David's destiny clearer than David did in his anger."},
{q:"What did David say of Abigail's counsel?", options:["Blessed be thy advice, which hast kept me this day from shedding blood","Thy words are foolish","I need no counsel","Go back to thy husband"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:33",verse:"And blessed be thy advice, and blessed be thou, which hast kept me this day from coming to shed blood, and from avenging myself with mine own hand.", insight:"Blessed be thy advice; David let a wise woman turn him from sin, and called it blessing."},
{q:"What happened to Nabal in the end?", options:["About ten days after, the LORD smote Nabal, that he died","David slew him with the sword","He repented and made peace","He fled to the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:38",verse:"And it came to pass about ten days after, that the LORD smote Nabal, that he died.", insight:"The LORD smote Nabal; when Abigail told him all in the morning his heart had already turned to stone, and God settled the account Himself."},
{q:"What did Abigail answer when David sent for her to be his wife?", options:["Let thine handmaid be a servant to wash the feet of the servants of my lord","I am unworthy","Ask my father","I will come as queen"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 25:41",verse:"And she arose, and bowed herself on her face to the earth, and said, Behold, let thine handmaid be a servant to wash the feet of the servants of my lord.", insight:"A servant to wash feet; Abigail's humility made her fit for a king's house, and she became his wife."}
]}
]);
